cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Honghu.jl in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Honghu.jl: three-dimensional radiation hydrodynamics in Julia"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Chong-Chong
    family-names: He
    email: chongchong.he@anu.edu.au
    affiliation: Australian National University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2332-8178"
    website: "https://chongchonghe.github.io/"
version: 0.1.0
# The concept DOI, which resolves to the latest version archived on Zenodo.
# Zenodo ignores this field when it archives a release, so it cannot clash
# with the DOI Zenodo gives each new version.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23569081
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/chongchonghe/Honghu.jl"
url: "https://chongchonghe.github.io/Honghu.jl/"
abstract: >-
  Honghu.jl is a three-dimensional radiation-hydrodynamics code in pure Julia.
  It solves the Euler equations with a method-of-lines finite-volume scheme
  (HLLC or LLF Riemann solvers, PCM, PLM or PPM reconstruction) coupled to
  two-moment (M1) radiation transport, grey or in frequency groups, with an HLL
  solver, an IMEX PD-ARS time integrator and an implicit matter-radiation
  coupling. It includes the adaptive reduced speed of light approximation and
  dust-gas thermal coupling, and serves as a test bed for algorithms developed
  for the Quokka code.
keywords:
  - radiation hydrodynamics
  - astrophysics
  - M1 closure
  - reduced speed of light approximation
  - finite-volume methods
  - Julia
